Are you ready for two days on a real trading floor?

Join the Flow Quant Trading Days at our Amsterdam office on 7 &amp; 8 December 2026 - a hands-on quant trading academy for a select group of 15 students. Find out whether trading is for you with an exciting look inside our Trading floor, and the chance to receive a full-time job offer as a Graduate Trader.

Over two days you'll price, arbitrage and hedge in live simulations, make markets under real time pressure, and go head-to-head with our traders in games built to test your instinct. You will have the opportunity to show your curiosity while shadowing the trading desks, watching news as it hits the market.

What's in it for you?

• An insight into trading at Flow Traders;

• Introductory classes on traditional finance, Crypto and ETFs;

• Hands-on simulations where you can show your competitive spirit;

• Desk shadowing in small groups;

• Games night to demonstrate your trading intuition - where you’ll go head-to-head with our traders;

• Our in-house facilities: gym with personal trainers, bar, barista, arcade room, and a lounge with daily catered lunches from our chef;

• Dinner in Amsterdam and farewell drinks in the Flow Bar with the trading team;

• And of course, the chance to receive a full-time job offer as a Graduate Trader.

Do you have what it takes?

Are you graduating in 2026 or 2027 from a BSc/MSc STEM degree in the Netherlands, with a demonstrable interest in trading on your CV? Do you code - Python or otherwise - and enjoy reasoning with probabilities and brainteasers? Can you spot an opportunity, and are you assertive enough to seize it? We're looking for competitive, curious and entrepreneurial students.

The application procedure

We invite you to apply through our website by submitting your resume as well as a persuasive cover letter. The application deadline will be November 13 th .

&nbsp;

Flow Traders does not accept unsolicited resumes from any professional staffing or search firms. All resumes, and any other information identifying potential candidates, submitted to any employee at Flow Traders via-email, the Internet or directly without a valid and signed search agreement will be deemed free to contact by Flow Traders without any restrictions and no placement fee of any kind will be paid in the event the candidate is hired by Flow Traders.

About WPP Media

WPP is the trusted growth partner for the world’s leading brands. With exceptional talent, trusted data and intelligence, and world-class partnerships - all united by our pioneering agentic marketing platform, WPP Open - we help clients navigate change, capture opportunity, and deliver transformational growth. 

WPP Media is WPP's AI-driven media operating unit, bringing together media, data, and partnerships to deliver creative personalisation at scale. Connected through WPP Open and powered by Open Intelligence, clients see exactly where, how, and why their media investment is working.

For more information, visit wppmedia.com .

Role Summary and Impact &nbsp;

As part of the Global Operations Centre (GOC) , you will work closely with teams across the United States, Europe, and Asia to deliver high-impact solutions in a collaborative, multicultural environment. We are looking for a Media Orchestrator who will: &nbsp;

• End-to-End Campaign Delivery &amp; Coordination &nbsp;
Manage campaign workflows from brief interpretation to post-campaign analysis while leading status calls, managing timelines, and keeping deliverables aligned across teams. &nbsp;

• DCO Tech Build &amp; Configuration &nbsp;
Configure, build, and maintain dynamic creative decision trees in DCO platforms to ensure audience, message, creative, and media rules execute accurately against strategy. &nbsp;

• Troubleshooting &amp; Performance Reporting &nbsp;
Identify and resolve technical, campaign, or creative issues promptly, while creating performance reports to extract actionable creative insights for optimization. &nbsp;

• New Business &amp; Market Enablement &nbsp;
Support pitches and market adoption by creating compelling case studies, workshop materials, and pitch collateral that highlight HVCS capabilities and success stories. &nbsp;

• Workflow Optimization &amp; AI Innovation &nbsp;
Leverage AI tools (such as WPP Open) and emerging DCO technologies to streamline production processes, reduce manual effort, and drive continuous workflow improvement. &nbsp;

&nbsp;

&nbsp;

Skills and Experience &nbsp;

• 2+ years' experience in Ad Operations, Digital Activation, Campaign Management or DCO platforms such as: Flashtalking/Innovid, Smartly, Celtra, etc. &nbsp;

• Advanced level of English (this will be assessed during the interview process) &nbsp;

• Bachelor’s degree &nbsp;

• Proven understanding of digital media channels and campaign delivery fundamentals, with hands-on experience using ad-serving and trafficking platforms. &nbsp;

• Comfortable working with campaign data, building performance reports, and applying str ong analytical skills to solve delivery challenges. &nbsp;

• Highly organized with sharp attention to detail, strong process management skills, and clear verbal and written communication. &nbsp;

&nbsp;

Life at WPP Media &amp; Benefits &nbsp;

Our passion for shaping the next era of media is powered by our commitment to   Be Extraordinary, investing in our employees to inspire transformational creativity. We also   Lead Optimistically, firmly believing in and   Championing Growth and Development   for every individual. This commitment allows WPP Media employees to leverage the extensive global WPP Media &amp; WPP networks to pursue their passions, build vital professional connections, and learn at the cutting edge of marketing and advertising. &nbsp; &nbsp;

We   Create an Open environment   built on trust and respect, where everyone feels they belong and has opportunities to progress. This inclusive culture is fostered through a variety of employee resource groups and frequent in-office events showcasing team wins, sharing thought leadership, and celebrating holidays and milestone events. Our comprehensive benefits package reflects this commitment, including competitive medical, group retirement plans, vision, and dental insurance, significant paid time off, preferential partner discounts, and employee mental health
